sub:Head {
  this: a np:Nanopublication ;
    np:hasAssertion sub:assertion ;
    np:hasProvenance sub:provenance ;
    np:hasPublicationInfo sub:pubinfo .
}

sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/physiology-laplace> a delphi:Concept, skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Laplace wall stress: pressure in a thin-walled vessel is limited by wall strength, thickness and radius (Lean 4, kernel-checked)" ;
    dct:description "The wall stress of a thin-walled sphere under pressure is P r / (2 t) and of a cylinder P r / t; stress grows with radius at fixed pressure and thickness, so a wall of strength sigma_max limits the pressure to 2 sigma_max t / r (sphere) or sigma_max t / r (cylinder)." ;
    dct:source "Proved in this project (lean/Delphi/Favored.lean) as an extension of the neutral case of Kimura (1962) to non-opposing selection; no paper states it in this form." ;
    skos:notation "sigma = P r / (2 t) <= sigma_max  =>  P <= 2 sigma_max t / r" ;
    skos:definition """/-- At fixed pressure and thickness, wall stress grows with radius. -/
theorem sphereWallStress_mono {P t r₁ r₂ : ℝ} (hP : 0 < P) (ht : 0 < t) (h : r₁ ≤ r₂) :
    sphereWallStress P r₁ t ≤ sphereWallStress P r₂ t"""^^delphi:lean4 ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    delphi:leanDeclaration "Delphi.Physiology.sphereWallStress" ;
    delphi:leanTheorem "Delphi.Physiology.sphereWallStress_mono", "Delphi.Physiology.laplace_pressure_limit", "Delphi.Physiology.hoop_pressure_limit" ;
    delphi:leanVerified "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    skos:scopeNote "Thin-wall idealisation, static, no bending or residual stress. No vessel radius, thickness or wall strength for any fish is in this project, so the bound is proved with no instance; it constrains nothing until those are measured." ;
    rdfs:comment "Status: kernel-checked (Lean 4 accepted the module with zero sorry and standard axioms only). Not expert-validated. Does not establish: anything about organisms. The theorem is exact inside the stated model and silent outside it; strict neutrality, constant population size, Wright-Fisher reproduction and independent mutant fates (Kimura), fixed fitnesses and haploid inheritance (Fisher), equal fecundity and a 1:1 sex ratio (Maynard Smith) are assumptions written in the module header, not conclusions. Kernel-checked is not expert-validated: no human expert has validated these statements. Whether the Lean statement faithfully renders the paper is a separate assessment record, and so far only one assessor provider has run." ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/delphisci/blob/3617fb32/lean/Delphi/Physiology.lean>, <https://delphi-mission-control.ashenoy000.workers.dev/t/lean/lean.json>, <https://delphi-mission-control.ashenoy000.workers.dev/t/lean/> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/physiology-laplace> dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/physiology-laplace> ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/lean-kernel-check-physiology-laplace> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/lean-kernel-check-physiology-laplace> a delphi:EvidenceItem ;
    rdfs:label "Lean 4 kernel accepted Delphi.Physiology.sphereWallStress_mono with zero sorry and standard axioms, and rejected 1 deliberately broken variant(s)" ;
    dct:description "Build receipt. Lean (version 4.35.0, x86_64-w64-windows-gnu, commit eb6cafb7290e8bd5f2937522d8d804f58f02bafc, Release); toolchain leanprover/lean4:v4.35.0; Mathlib v4.35.0 (56a005855ea17e0b0958f73ec801ae140b0a1679). lake build exit 0 in 23.2 s with 0 errors; 0 sorry in lean/Delphi/Physiology.lean (66 lines). #print axioms for Delphi.Physiology.sphereWallStress_mono, Delphi.Physiology.laplace_pressure_limit, Delphi.Physiology.hoop_pressure_limit: Classical.choice, Quot.sound, propext only (Lean's standard axioms; no sorryAx). Mutation evidence (lean/mutate.mjs, 2026-10-31T21:58:20.213Z): 1 deliberate change(s) to the statement or the model were each rejected by the compiler: [laplace-factor-dropped] Statement strengthened by dropping the factor 2: a sphere claimed to hold at most sigma_max t / r, the cylinder bound. Stronger than the wall stress allows, so the proof must fail. Rejected with 1 error(s): Physiology.lean:55:2: error: linarith failed to find a contradiction Controls: 16 of 16 unmodified modules accepted by the same command." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/physiology-laplace> ;
    rdfs:comment "This evidence item establishes that the stated theorem follows from the stated model. Does not establish: anything about organisms. The theorem is exact inside the stated model and silent outside it; strict neutrality, constant population size, Wright-Fisher reproduction and independent mutant fates (Kimura), fixed fitnesses and haploid inheritance (Fisher), equal fecundity and a 1:1 sex ratio (Maynard Smith) are assumptions written in the module header, not conclusions. Kernel-checked is not expert-validated: no human expert has validated these statements. Whether the Lean statement faithfully renders the paper is a separate assessment record, and so far only one assessor provider has run." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://delphi-mission-control.ashenoy000.workers.dev/t/lean/lean.json>, <https://github.com/fractastical/delphisci/blob/3617fb32/lean/mutations.json>, <https://github.com/fractastical/delphisci/blob/3617fb32/lean/Delphi/Audit.lean> .
}

